    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n6D1E813DD98BAB2A538D5D2B4954BCAA2C7CDC59A36DF8772AE5435535A74863EABD98ECA8C0\n\n### qTox Version\n\nlatest\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n_No response_\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.22\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.4.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox\n2. start audio call\n3. network is still connected, but packets are getting stuck or some other problem inside network, while local connection is still active and working (hard to reproduce, I know)\n4. call timeouts (or something) and thus it ends the call. while this can clearly be seen (that it ends) while you are looking on qTox, when you are not, there is **no hang-up sound** (as it normally is and should be)\n\nthis does not happen always, it happens only when there is some disconnection/interruption in WAN as when there is other disconnection in LAN, it plays hang-up sound.\n\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nIn the logs, there is just that \"`Call with <nick> ended unexpectedly. Call duration: <time>`\"\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nhang-up sound in every case when call ends\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlmost always\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```",
